[asy]
size(150);
draw((0,0)--(0,20)..(1,19.5)..(2,20)--(2,0)..(1,-.5)..(0,0),linewidth(1));
draw((0,20)..(1,20.5)..(2,20),linewidth(1));
draw((1,19.5)--(0,18.5),linewidth(1));
draw((2,.5)--(1,-.5),linewidth(1));
draw((2,16)--(0,14),linewidth(1));
draw((2,11)--(0,9),linewidth(1));

draw((2,6)--(0,4),linewidth(1));

[/asy]

Stuart has drawn a pair of concentric circles, as shown.  He draws chords $\overline{AB}$, $\overline{BC}, \ldots$ of the large circle, each tangent to the small one.  If $m\angle ABC=75^\circ$, then how many segments will he draw before returning to his starting point at $A$? [asy]
size(100); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8));
real rad1 = 1/Sin(37.5);
draw(Circle(origin,1)); draw(Circle(origin,rad1));
pair A = rad1*dir(190), B = rad1*dir(190 + 105), C = rad1*dir(190 + 2*105), D = rad1*dir(190 + 315);
draw(A--B--C--D,EndArrow(size=5));
label("$A$",A,W); label("$B$",B,S); label("$C$",C,E);
[/asy]

In the diagram below, $\|\overrightarrow{OA}\| = 1,$ $\|\overrightarrow{OB}\| = 1,$ and $\|\overrightarrow{OC}\| = \sqrt{2}.$  Also, $\tan \angle AOC = 7$ and $\angle BOC = 45^\circ.$

[asy]
unitsize(2 cm);

pair A, B, C, O;

A = (1,0);
B = (-0.6,0.8);
C = (0.2,1.4);
O = (0,0);

draw(O--A,Arrow(6));
draw(O--B,Arrow(6));
draw(O--C,Arrow(6));

label("$A$", A, E);
label("$B$", B, NW);
label("$C$", C, N);
label("$O$", O, S);
[/asy]

